    <string name="block_unverified">Block calls without a verified number marker</string>
    <string name="block_unverified_hint">The marker (STIR/SHAKEN) is carrier-side verification. It is rarely sent in Russia, so enabling this is not recommended: your own contacts would be blocked too.</string>

    <string name="counters_blocked">Blocked calls: %1$d</string>

    <string name="section_about">How it works</string>
    <string name="about_text">Android hands the app an incoming call before the phone starts ringing. The app compares the number with your address book and rejects the call when the number is not there. Everything happens on the phone: no internet is needed and no data leaves the device.\n\nCall screening apps never receive hidden or private numbers — Android does not pass them. To cover those as well, turn on unknown caller blocking in the Phone app.</string>

